<%# The markup for a stimulus-autocomplete field: visible text input, the
    hidden field holding the chosen record's id, and the (initially empty)
    <ul> the library fills with suggestions.

    Fields migrated off typeahead.js render this instead of repeating the
    wrapper's data-* attributes. Markup, labels and classes are kept
    identical to what the original typeahead.js fields emitted, so the GUI
    is unchanged - only the JS driving the dropdown is different. The
    server-side resolvers are unchanged too: they don't know or care which
    JS widget populated these fields.

    Required locals:
      f            - the form builder, used for the hidden id field
      id_attribute - the model attribute holding the id, e.g. :author_id
      input_id     - dom id of the visible input (other JS still keys off
                     these, e.g. app/views/names/update.js.erb)
      input_name   - param name of the visible input, e.g.
                     "name[author_typeahead]"
      input_value  - what to show in the visible input on page load
      label        - the field's label text
      title        - the input's title/tooltip text
      url          - endpoint rendering shared/_autocomplete_suggestions

    Optional locals:
      wrapper_class   - extra class(es) on the wrapper div
      input_class     - extra class(es) on the visible input, e.g.
                        "requires-rank"
      required        - marks the input required and adds the red asterisk
                        the app's other mandatory fields carry
      label_suffix    - text rendered after the </label>, e.g. a field's
                        "[help text]" note
      extra_params    - hash of static params added to every request, see
                        the autocomplete controller's buildURL
      live_params     - hash of param name => dom id, read from the page at
                        query time; for a field whose suggestions depend on
                        another field the user can still change (e.g. the
                        Parent field sending the currently selected rank)
      term_delimiter  - cut the typed text at this string before querying,
                        for fields whose suggestions are displayed as
                        "<name> | <rank> | ..." and so get typed back with
                        that trailing detail attached
      dependents_field - element id to hand to window.setDependents after a
                         pick; omit unless the field has dependents
      min_length      - characters before suggestions are fetched (default 1)

    The hidden field must sit inside the wrapper for the library to find
    the target, and is rendered through the form builder so it keeps the
    conventional "name_author_id"-style dom id that other JS and the tests
    rely on. %>
<% wrapper_class = local_assigns.fetch(:wrapper_class, nil) %>
<% input_class = local_assigns.fetch(:input_class, nil) %>
<% required = local_assigns.fetch(:required, false) %>
<% label_suffix = local_assigns.fetch(:label_suffix, nil) %>
<% extra_params = local_assigns.fetch(:extra_params, {}) %>
<% live_params = local_assigns.fetch(:live_params, {}) %>
<% term_delimiter = local_assigns.fetch(:term_delimiter, nil) %>
<% dependents_field = local_assigns.fetch(:dependents_field, nil) %>
<% min_length = local_assigns.fetch(:min_length, 1) %>
<div class="form-group autocomplete <%= wrapper_class %>"
     data-controller="autocomplete"
     data-action="autocomplete.change->autocomplete#syncDependents"
     data-autocomplete-url-value="<%= url %>"
     data-autocomplete-query-param-value="term"
     data-autocomplete-min-length-value="<%= min_length %>"
     data-autocomplete-extra-params-value="<%= extra_params.to_json %>"
     data-autocomplete-live-params-value="<%= live_params.to_json %>"
     data-autocomplete-term-delimiter-value="<%= term_delimiter %>"
     data-autocomplete-dependents-field-value="<%= dependents_field %>"
     role="combobox">
  <label for="<%= input_id %>"><%= label %><% if required %><span class="red">*</span><% end %></label><%= label_suffix %><br>
  <input id="<%= input_id %>"
         name="<%= input_name %>"
         class="typeahead form-control <%= input_class %>"
         type="text"
         title="<%= title %>"
         tabindex="<%= increment_tab_index %>"
         <%= "required" if required %>
         data-autocomplete-target="input"
         value="<%= input_value %>"/>
  <%= f.hidden_field(id_attribute, data: { "autocomplete-target": "hidden" }) %>
  <ul class="autocomplete-results" data-autocomplete-target="results"></ul>
</div>
